{
  "about": "XDesk's gesture table as recorded touch sequences (INPUT.md §3, §9). Every implementation runs these: input-core's JVM tests (GestureVectorsTest) and, later, the web display. Events: [kind, time ms, pointer index, [[id, x, y], ...], tool]; [\"wait\", time] only lets time pass. Positions are pixels at the given density. Expected output is summarised: moves in a row are one \"move\", scroll changes in a row one \"scroll change dx dy\" in wheel steps (dy > 0 is the wheel turning down) summed to one decimal, momentum frames one \"scroll momentum\", a press right before its release a \"click\", repeated move frames one; vibrations are left out.",
  "tuning": {
    "density": 1,
    "longPressMs": 400,
    "doubleTapMs": 300,
    "slopDp": 8,
    "scrollStepDp": 28,
    "naturalScroll": true
  },
